A||N||9||Freshj||To EGR or not to EGR||||1||
Z||000000||Freshj||12-13-2001||11:07 PM||||I was reading someplace, on the forum probably, about removing the EGR valve. I'm in a non emissions testing state, so I'm not too worried about that. I was wondering how this is done and if it's even possiable. And if it is, what advantage do you get? It would be on my 86 SE.||||reg||1
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-13-2001||11:40 PM||||I have yet to see any significant gains from removing all egr equipment, other than it cleans up and simplifies the engine bay<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||12-13-2001||11:41 PM||||However, it would be encouraging to see dyno results from similarly equiped cars - one with all EGR equipment, and one where EGR is deleted<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||12-13-2001||11:58 PM||||When the ecm calls for the egr operation, it adds up to 9.5 degrees of timing and can pull almost 25% of the fuel from the fuel map. Is it worth it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Freshj||12-14-2001||12:14 AM||||I'm taking it that its a good plan to remove it. Anybody know whats involved in removing everything?||||reg||3
Z||000005||Joe Torma||12-14-2001||02:03 AM||||And when the ECM calls for it and it isn't there...then what?<P>If you delete it from the chip go for it.<P>When you romp on it(WOT) it doesn't operate(closes) anyway.  So why do you want to get rid of it?<P>I agree its a POS part that fails, I even deleted it from my 3400, but if your computer is programmed to operate with it, I think it needs to be there.  Yeah, there's people that say its going to give you 20hp, but I bet its because it was busted and needed repair. <P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||johnt671||12-14-2001||07:58 AM||||I pluged the vacume line on my 84 to try it.  Seemed to run a bit smoother and felt a bit better throttle response.  A bit later I picked up a throttle body with way less miles on it and put it on my car.  When I took the gasket off under the T.B. I found the passages were completely plugged up with carbon.  Hooked up the EGR and tried it again.  Now I don't feel any difference in the response.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroPerformance||12-14-2001||05:03 PM||||I capped mine off because the tube broke. I passed emissions just fine without it. The car idles better and the "Check Engine" light doesn't come on all the time anymore.<P>I don't know if I gained power because I added a performance cam and high compression pistons at the same time.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||BMWTECH's Fiero GT||12-15-2001||12:47 AM||||I'm not sure how you guys are removing the EGR with no adverse effects.  Sure the EGR valve is an emission component that lowers NOX by adding exhaust back into the combustion chamber, but it also serves a dual purpose to keep the combustion chamber cooler (that's how it lowers nox).  Usually if you take a vehicle designed for EGR and delete it, idle will not be affected (because EGR is not introduced at idle), and you probably will still pass emission test due to the light requirements of pre OBD 2 vehicles.  However there will be a problem of detonation at cruising speeds due to the increased combustion chamber temps, if severe enough this can really do some damage to the pistons.  The only fix for the detonation would be a timing change that would negate any horsepower increses from removing the EGR in the first place.  Just my opinion, but I don't see any reason to remove the valve.||||reg||1
Z||000009||lou_dias||12-15-2001||07:07 PM||||On my stock 88 GT, the only drivability issues I have is when I take my foot off the pedal below 1800 rpm.<BR>I'm sure it's because the computer isn't reacting properly to all the extra air it has and goes back and forth from lean to rich and back again.<P>I'm sure a proper chip could eliminate this.<BR>My timing is retarded 2 degrees and I still make lots more power than with the egr and stock timing.<P>I hate to say it but it feels like as much hp as my agressive 3.4 rebuild (147rwhp), though it doesn't have the torque, but it's not that far off really.<P>When I get my fresh 3.4 back, I will be promptly removing the EGR.||||reg||1
